From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt DeVillier <matt.devillier@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 17:18:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] UefiPayloadPkg: Unregister the setup hotkey before clearing
 the prompt

[ouroBIOS: commit 1817a2bc4ae8 of MrChromebox's edk2, as it is]

The timeout path cleared the "Press ESC" line and then dropped the key
notify. The clear's GOP Blt lowers TPL on the way out and flushes queued
key notifications, so an ESC pressed as the prompt disappeared still ran
the callback and painted "Entering Setup..." into the strip that had just
been wiped. Unregister first so that flush cannot redraw the line.

Signed-off-by: Matt DeVillier <matt.devillier@gmail.com>
---
 .../Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBootManager.c        | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBootManager.c b/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBootManager.c
index b235733a4715da316d3486362d686f837448e018..bb78bb9f44fd1c607eddef73bbc6937c7d88947b 100644
--- a/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBootManager.c
+++ b/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBootManager.c
@@ -589,8 +589,8 @@ PlatformBootManagerWaitCallback (
   )
 {
   if (TimeoutRemain == 0) {
-    BootLogoClearProgress ();
     PlatformUnregisterBootManagerEntryNotifyCallback ();
+    BootLogoClearProgress ();
   }
 
   return;
